---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import AboutHeroImage from '../assets/knight.jpg';
import HollowImage from '../assets/hollow.jpg';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="My lore"
	pubDate={new Date('August 08 2000')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<p>
		Long ago, the world of Aethoria was a land of thriving kingdoms, soaring citadels, and ancient magic. At its heart stood the Eternal Spire, a colossal tower said to bind the realms together and channel the life force of the world itself. Under its light, humanity prospered, and the great races lived in an uneasy peace.
	</p>
	<p>
		But prosperity bred ambition.
	</p>
	<p>
		The Seven Kings, hungry for immortality and power, sought to control the Spire's magic. Their scholars and sorcerers delved into forbidden arts, tearing open seals that had remained untouched since the dawn of creation. In their arrogance, they awakened an ancient force known only as The Hollow King, a being imprisoned before history was written.
	</p>
	<p>
		The war that followed became known as The Sundering.
	</p>
	<p>
		Mountains split apart, oceans swallowed cities, and the skies burned for seven years. Entire kingdoms vanished beneath ash and darkness. Though the Hollow King was ultimately defeated, the damage could not be undone. The Eternal Spire shattered, scattering fragments of its power across the world.
	</p>
	<p>
		Centuries later, Aethoria remains a broken land.
	</p>
	<p>
		The great kingdoms are dust and ruin. Monsters roam roads once guarded by proud armies. Forgotten machines and magical relics lie buried beneath collapsed cities. Small settlements cling to survival behind crumbling walls while rival warlords fight over scraps of the old world.
	</p>
	<p>
		Many believe the age of heroes is long over.
	</p>
	<p>
		Yet some still wander the ruined roads in search of hope.
	</p>
	<p>
		Among them is Sir Aldric of the Ashen Road, a knight without a kingdom. Armed with a weathered longsword and guided by fading legends, he journeys across the fallen world seeking the scattered fragments of the Eternal Spire. For whispers carried on the wind speak of a terrible truth:
	</p>
	<p>
		The Hollow King was never truly destroyed.
	</p>
	<p>
		And deep beneath the ruins of Aethoria, something is beginning to awaken once more.
	</p>
	<Image src={HollowImage} alt="The Hollow King" />
</Layout>
